<Page title="About ClearCove Pools: Free Pool Care Guides and Tools" description="ClearCove Pools is a free site built around a simple pool chemistry calculator and care guides, so you can stop guessing at chemicals.">
  <p>{site.BRAND} is an independent site. {site.author.bio}</p>

  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>Most pool owners overdose chlorine or ignore total alkalinity until the water turns cloudy. The calculator on this site takes your pool volume, current test strip readings, and target ranges, then tells you how much chlorine, muriatic acid, or soda ash to add, in ounces or pounds, not vague fractions of a bottle.</p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>Our chemistry ranges come from the Pool & Hot Tub Alliance's water balance guidelines and manufacturer dosing charts for common chemicals. Guides are drafted with AI assistance and checked against those charts before publishing, a process our <a href="/editorial/">editorial policy</a> covers. We test the calculator's math against known dosing scenarios rather than assuming the formula is right.</p>

  <h2>How we make money</h2>
  <p>The calculator and guides are free. We earn affiliate commissions when readers buy test kits, chemicals, or pool equipment through links on this site, as spelled out in our <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a>.</p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>If a dosing range or calculator result looks off, use <a href="/contact/">contact</a>. We check it, correct it, and date the fix.</p>
</Page>
